{color.GG}LLSI {color.N}is a system loader within the {color.GG}Ares Framework {color.N}designed to load all registered LLSI modules.
These modules are loaded last in the startup sequence, which means they can overwrite the users {color.BB}~/.aresrc {color.N}and {color.BB}~/.ares/init/shmod{color.N}.

{color.YY}Warning{color.N}:
    {color.R}- {color.N}Environment Overwrite:
      {color.WW}LLSI modules can overwrite {color.GG}~/.aresrc{color.WW}, {color.GG}~/.ares/init/shmod{color.WW}, and the {color.GG}global shell environment{color.WW}.{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.N}Potential Conflicts:
      {color.WW}Conflicts may occur if an LLSI module attempts to overwrite a function or variable that has been locked ({color.GG}readonly{color.WW}).{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.N}No Comments Support:
      {color.WW}The {color.GG}init/llsi.init {color.WW}file does not support comment syntax of any kind.{color.N}

Syntax Format ({color.BB}init/llsi.init{color.N}):
{color.R}your{color.DG}::{color.R}lib{color.DG}::{color.GG}name {color.N}{
    key {color.GG}-> {color.YY}source{color.N}
    key {color.GG}-> {color.YY}source{color.N}
}

Real Example:
{color.R}your{color.DG}::{color.R}lib{color.DG}::{color.GG}name {color.N}{
    runtime.{color.BB}init {color.GG}-> {color.YY}lib/shell/myinit.llsi{color.N}
    runtime.{color.BB}free {color.GG}-> {color.YY}lib/shell/myfree.llsi{color.N}
}

Declaration Guidelines:
{color.N}It is recommended to lock functions and variables ({color.GG}readonly{color.N}) to prevent them from being overwritten.
Exporting is optional and should be used if you want the functions or variables to be accessible in subshells/scripts, not just the current shell session.

For Functions:
{color.PP}readonly {color.GG}-{color.N}f {color.R}yourfunc{color.N}
{color.PP}export {color.GG}-{color.N}f {color.R}yourfunc    {color.DG}# Optional: required only if needed in sub-scripts{color.N}

For Variables:
{color.PP}readonly {color.R}myval{color.GG}={color.N}val
{color.PP}export {color.R}myval    {color.DG}# Optional: required only if needed in sub-scripts{color.N}